    "title": "Complete & Unbelievable: The Otis Redding Dictionary of Soul",
    "description": "1966 studio album by Otis Redding",
    "extract": "Complete & Unbelievable: The Otis Redding Dictionary of Soul, or simply Dictionary of Soul, is the fifth studio album by the American soul singer-songwriter Otis Redding and his last solo studio album released before his death. The successful Otis Blue and the following performance at Whisky a Go Go led to his rising fame across the United States. The first side of the album mainly contains cover versions, and the second songs mainly written by Redding.",
